          "final_text_tail": "The implementation is complete and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a flexible `validate_input` method to `ToolCalls` in `dspy/adapters/types/tool.py` that normalizes varied LM output formats into the canonical `tool_calls` structure.\n\n**Changes:**\n1. Added `import json` and `import pydantic` to the imports.\n2. Added a `validate_input` classmethod (a `@pydantic.model_validator(mode=\"before\")`) to `ToolCalls` that handles:\n   - **Canonical form** \u2013 dict with `tool_calls` key \u2192 returned as-is\n   - **Single object** \u2013 dict with `name`/`args` (no `tool_calls`) \u2192 wrapped into `{\"tool_calls\": [data]}`\n   - **Bare list** \u2013 list of dicts \u2192 wrapped into `{\"tool_calls\": data}`\n   - **JSON strings** \u2013 parsed via `json.loads`; if it parses to a dict/list, the result is normalized through the same logic above\n   - **Non-JSON strings** \u2013 returned unchanged\n\nThe method returns plain Python structures (dict/list/string), never a `ToolCalls` instance, per the spec \u2014 consistent with the `validate_input` pattern already used by `Code`, `Audio`, and `Image`.\n\nAll 88 existing adapter tests pass (26 in `test_tool.py` specifically).",
