          "final_text_tail": "The task is complete. The implementation:\n\n1. **`_canonicalize_args`** helper (module-level, line 20): recursively sorts dict keys, converts tuples\u2192lists, trims string whitespace, preserves numeric/bool types.\n\n2. **Fingerprint generation** in `ToolCall.__init__`: canonicalizes args, builds `{\"name\": ..., \"args\": ...}`, serializes with `json.dumps(sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\",\":\"))`, hashes with sha256. `fingerprint` (64-char hex) and `id` (first 8 chars) are set at creation.\n\n3. Both `fingerprint` and `id` are pydantic fields with `\"\"` defaults, set once in `__init__`. The tool name is included in the fingerprint input (per clarifications), while the canonicalized args themselves contain only args.\n\nVerified: identical calls with different key order / tuple-vs-list / whitespace produce the same 64-char fingerprint and 8-char id. All 36 existing tool tests pass.",
